# L'AmourSucré - core rules

Static bilingual bakery site (Next.js App Router). No backend, DB, or auth.

## Ownership of code

- Copy → `src/lib/dictionaries/{en,fr}.ts` only (typed by `types.ts`)
- Prices / catalog → `src/lib/menu.ts`
- Contact / ops constants → `src/lib/site.ts`
- Photo paths → `src/lib/photos.ts` (components use keys, never raw paths)
- Layout / UI → `src/components/`
- Routes → `src/app/[locale]/`
- Owner docs → `docs/` (update when structure or rules change)

## Hard constraints

- Never hard-code EN/FR customer copy inside components
- Never duplicate prices as strings in dictionaries
- Every new string/item/photo needs both languages; build must fail closed
- `"use client"` only when state/effects/browser APIs are required
- Design system is bone / brass / ink (`globals.css`); do not casually restore pastel tokens
- Do not add `src/app/api/`, CMS, or auth unless replacing the mailto model
- Do not commit secrets, private keys, passwords, private IPs, or internal hostnames (see `docs/SECURITY.md` and `.cursor/rules/secrets.mdc`)
- Do not commit unoptimised multi-MB photos
- Prefer small, purposeful diffs - no drive-by refactors
- Never use the Unicode em dash (U+2014); use ASCII `-` or rephrase (hooks enforce)

